\item sensitivity (the share of human positives the judge called positive) and
specificity, with Wilson intervals, and the half-width of the
sensitivity interval;
\item the swap-inconsistency rate: the share of judged items whose verdict
changed with the presentation order, with a Wilson interval (\code{NA} for a
one-order judge). Swap inconsistency is the position-bias measure of
Zheng et al. (2023).
